# Copy to .env and change both values
CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=change-me-clickhouse
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-grafana
# Optional. Address the OTLP ports 4317 and 4318 are published on: 127.0.0.1 = this PC only, 0.0.0.0 = LAN (default).
# On Linux, Docker bypasses ufw/firewalld for published ports, so this is what limits access.
# OTLP_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Optional. Address Grafana (port 3000) is published on: 127.0.0.1 = this PC only (default), 0.0.0.0 = LAN.
# setup-server.sh on Linux sets it to 0.0.0.0 unless you pass --local-only.
# GRAFANA_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Optional. Host port of Grafana (default 3000); use another one when 3000 is taken. The Windows script assumes 3000.
# GRAFANA_PORT=3000
# Optional. ClickHouse image tag (default 25.8). setup-server.sh sets 22.3.20.29 on ARM CPUs without lrcpc (Raspberry Pi 4; ClickHouse needs ARMv8.2 since 22.10).
# Changing it between 22.3 and a newer version on a volume with data needs dump, new volume, restore: setup-server.sh refuses and prints the steps.
# CLICKHOUSE_VERSION=25.8
# Optional. Days the data is kept (default 365). setup-server.sh writes 180 with ClickHouse 22.3 (Raspberry Pi 4) and keeps the value afterwards.
# A shorter value deletes the rows older than that when setup-server.sh applies it (it asks first, --update dumps first).
# RETENTION_DAYS=365
# Optional. small = memory, thread and merge limits of a small server (clickhouse/limits/small/), none = ClickHouse defaults (default).
# CLICKHOUSE_LIMITS=none
# Optional. CPU cores of the ClickHouse container, 0 = no limit (default). setup-server.sh writes 2 with ClickHouse 22.3.
# CLICKHOUSE_CPUS=0
